    "q-84690": {
      "dom_id": "step-q84690",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "A coin is biased so that the probability of it landing on heads is $0.7.$ The coin is tossed $15$ times. What is the mean number of times the coin lands on heads?",
      "worked_solution": "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of times the coin lands on heads. \n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=15$ tosses\n\n- the probability of landing on heads for each toss is $p=0.7$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(15,0.7).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the mean is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the mean of the number of times the coin lands on heads is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\  & =(15)(0.7) \\\\  & =10.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
