    "q-130753": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130753",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "A restaurant knows that $13%$ of reservations are canceled by the customer. If the restaurant receives $30$ reservations, what is the mean number of canceled reservations?",
      "worked_solution": "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of canceled reservations.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=30$ reservations\n\n- the probability that a reservation is canceled is $p=13%=0.13$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(30,0.13).$ \n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the mean is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the mean number of canceled reservations is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\  & =(30)(0.13) \\\\  & =3.9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
