    "q-130760": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130760",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The probability that a product of a company is defective is $0.04.$ Random samples of $50$ products are taken from the week's production. What is the variance of the number of defective products in the sample?",
      "worked_solution": "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of defective products.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=50$ products in the sample\n\n- the probability that a product is defective is $p=0.04$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(50,0.04).$ \n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p),\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\n So, the variance of the number of defective products is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =(50)(0.04)(1-0.04) \\\\  & =(50)(0.04)(0.96) \\\\  & =1.92.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
