    "q-130759": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130759",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "A restaurant knows that $15%$ of reservations are not honored, which means the group doesn't arrive. If the restaurant receives $30$ reservations, what is the variance of the number of groups that do not arrive?",
      "worked_solution": "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of groups that do not arrive.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=30$ reservations\n\n- the probability that a group doesn't arrive is $p=15%=0.15$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(30,0.15).$ \n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p),\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\n So, the variance of the number of groups that do not arrive is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =(30)(0.15)(1-0.15) \\\\  & =(30)(0.15)(0.85) \\\\  & =3.825.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
