    "q-130884": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130884",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "A basketball player has a $70%$ success rate in shooting from the free throw line during a season. The player has ten shots from the free throw line in one match. What is the standard deviation of the number of successful free throws? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of successful free throws.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=10$ shots from the free throw line in the match\n\n- the probability that the player is successful from the free throw line  is $p=70%=0.7$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(10,0.7).$ \n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the standard deviation is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]}=\\sqrt{np(1-p)},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the standard deviation   of the number of successful free throws is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{np(1-p)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(10)(0.7)(1-0.7)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(10)(0.7)(0.3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2.1} \\\\  & ≈1.449\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
